      "statusChangeID": "6908dcccaaef5852e9c43f4b",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Unfortunately, a toggle is not possible to implement from a technical perspective (Unity does not support this).\n\nSteam Audio will ship, but we have some time left to make adjustments - as such, if you have *specific* feedback or concerns, please open dedicated cannys for that.\n\nNote that for things like \"Sound Direction\", a period of adjustments has to be considered. Usually, after using Steam Audio for a few hours, users report equal or even improved ability to perceive directionality. That said, it can be a bit subjective depending on your ears - not something we can make perfect for everyone, sadly.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-10-31T09:12:27.344Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Honestly, I don't think we should implement the Audio Beta feature yet. The reason is that it still seems functionally incomplete. Introducing it in its current state would cause significant changes to information like sound direction compared to before, and I feel it would place a greater burden on users than before. At the very least, I'd like to see either a feature implemented to revert audio settings to the current version's settings, or further improvements to the functionality, before introducing it.",
